# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ALLOWLIST .gitignore  —  ignore everything, then re-include what is public.
#
# This repository is PUBLIC: GitHub Pages serves it anonymously at
# thomasrandles.github.io/canslim-tracker. It also lives inside a working
# directory that contains a live Notion integration token in ~26 files
# (legacy notion_*/fix_*/cleanup_* scripts, Archive/, and the
# claude_desktop_config*.json backups, which additionally hold
# OPENAPI_MCP_HEADERS).
#
# A denylist could not hold that line: every new script written in this folder
# would be publishable by default, and one `git add -A` would leak the token.
# Hence the inversion below — new files are private unless named here.
#
# After editing this file, ALWAYS verify with:   git add -An
# Nothing containing a credential may appear in that output.
# ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# 1 ─ ignore every top-level entry
/*

# 2 ─ repo infrastructure
!/.gitignore
!/.nojekyll
!/.github/

# 3 ─ published dashboards (the actual product of this repo)
!/index.html
!/CANSLIM_Dashboard.html
!/Options_Dashboard.html

# 4 ─ orchestrators and screeners that carry no credentials
!/run_daily.bat
!/run_options_scan.bat
!/screen_stocks.py
!/scan_options.py
!/gen_options_html.py

# 5 ─ DayTrader subtree (governed by DayTrader/.gitignore)
!/DayTrader/

# 6 ─ belt and braces: never publish these even if a rule above widens.
#     Credentials live in .env; compiled bytecode embeds string constants.
.env
market_state.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
notion_writer.py
generate_dashboard.py
canslim_config.py
backup_pre_audit_*/
backup_claude_mcp_system/
claude_desktop_config*.json
backup_pre_batch2_*/
